    "created_at": "2019-12-12T14:41:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-12-12T14:41:58Z",
    "body": "Oh, I see. I thought \"none\" was an allowed value, but it's not.\r\n\r\nFor COOP, the rationale to have an allowed keyword for the default is to make it possible to change the default in the future. Do we envision that the default for COEP will stay the same?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
